A||N||13||AgaricX||Droppin in a Cadillac||||1||
Z||000000||AgaricX||12-01-2001||05:06 PM||||Ok... my 3800 SC project is about as mechanically done as it's going to get for awhile...  Mostly body work remains so I'm going to start grabbing info on my next project.<P>I see articles (ie BubbaJoe) with a 4.9L Caddy engine installed in a Fiero.  Also, I see the 4.6L Northstars in a few.  Which is preferrable?  I would think N* but which is easier (less modification).  I had to remachine the flywheel and manufacture new motor mounts to get my 3800SC in there... I'm sure I'll see more of the same?<P>Are there issues installing a N*?  I hear that people are still working out bugs and problems.  I'm really looking for POWER and RELIABILITY.  Period.  When its in, I wanna just keep it tuned and cleaned and not have to worry about it.  (Plus I want ricers and Mustangers to wet their pants)<P>Is there a difference between the different 4.6 N*s?  I was looking at edmunds.com and some (Eldorado, STS) output 300HP.  Some (SeVille) output 270HP.  IS this a difference in engines or other facotrs in the car?<P>Is it possible to retain a 5spd manual with the Caddy conversions?  I have a strong aversion to automatic transmissions.<P>BTW - You guys are the SOLE reason I have found my dreamcar (for under $75K).<P>I LOVE THIS CAR!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Homicidal||12-01-2001||05:21 PM||||is that car in your sig really your car or altered in Photoshop?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||12-01-2001||05:55 PM||||You can put a manual to a northstar, as artherd and Will can testify to.The difference in the N* engines is as you mentioned the horsepower but also the final gear ratio in the tranny.  If you are staying auto (I don't think you are) then you have to match ecm, engine and tranny.  I've had my N* for almost 2 years with no real problems, just waterpump and starter.  It's been fun and fast!  Get yourself a Cadillac Instrument cluster so you can scan the ecm!  <A HREF="http://members.rogers.com/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>http://members.rogers.com/jaygrande</A>  to see my N* page<BR>or <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598567222&r=0&t=0&showTutorial=0&ed=1007254555&indexURL=0&rd=1" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598567222&r=0&t=0&showTutorial=0&ed=1007254555&indexURL=0&rd=1</A> <BR>to see my car on ebay.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||12-01-2001||06:02 PM||||If you have any questions on the Caddy in a Fiero,ask rockcrawl,if he can't answer it,it can't be answered!  ||||reg||14
Z||000004||AgaricX||12-01-2001||06:23 PM||||Homicidal - Yes to both.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-03-2001||04:00 AM||||Well, you can actually use a plain 88 flywheel and clutch in a Northstar (the bolt pattern of the motors is the *same* right down to the clutch mounting surface on the rear-main-seal.) You'll have to have it drilled for <P>You have to notch the tranny webbing ($50 air grinder and 20min is all you need.)<P>You need at *least* a $1300 aftermarket ECU to use a 5-speed (still totally worth it!)<P>That really is about it, other than the usual connecting up all the lines, etc. (same old misc engine swap stuff, if you've done one before, especially a 3800, this'll be cake!)<P>The 4.9 caddy is much easier and cheaper...<BR>But! only 215hp.  and it *RED LINES* at 4500.<P>Compare that to 300bhp at 6k with a RED LINE OF 6750!<P>Don't expect to do a good looking N* swap for less than $5k, but OH the rewards of a good one!!!!<P>(yes, there are two slightly different Northstars. LD8 and L37.  The L37 is the 300hp/295lb-ft model. the LD8 is 275hp/300lb-ft  the *only* difference in the motor itsel as far as I can tell, is 5degrees intake cam timing (you could probally change this. Could probally advance even more for a really nice peaky engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hope this helps, boy that photoshop drawing looks great, BUILD IT MAN!Q  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||Nashco||12-03-2001||04:13 AM||||GROUND BREAKING NEWS!!!<P>I'm a member of the DIY-EFI mailing list (do it yourself fuel injection), and somebody recently made this post:<P>"I am transplanting a Cadillac N* V8 into a Fiero for use with a manual<BR>transmission.<BR>I have discovered a chap who has done the same thing, and is using an <BR>engine-management-only PROM he got from someone deep inside GM. The source <BR>for these PROMS can be considered dried up. I am going to ask him to <BR>download the contents of the PROM from his car to his PC, then e-mail me the <BR>file. What program does he need to do this? Once I have this file, where can <BR>I procure the software/hardware I need to burn it to a PROM?"<P>I have already emailed him pointing him to the forum, explaining there are MANY MANY owners out there who are in dire need of this information.  I was going to go 3800 SC, but if this PROM file gets put onto a computer so it can propogate, I wouldn't blink an eye before going N*.<P>I hope to hear back from him very soon.  If I don't hear from him in the next couple of days, I will email him again.  Whoever has this source code is now to be considered a Felon to PFF.  He is wanted, alive and able to talk!<P>In preparation for our hopefully incoming hailed guest, who wants to post the best possible way to get this PROM file?  Or, if the original source will burn a copy and send it off (to keep things anonymous if necessary) who has the chip reader for the northstar chips and can copy the PROM for us??<P>This is a HUGE development, and I'll be COMPLETELY grateful if we can make it happen.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
